Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.00,0:00:10.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Which high-impact papers are worth replicating —\Nand has anyone actually checked them?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:16.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,The OpenAIRE Graph can't tell you.\NReplication Radar can.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.00,0:00:27.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Search a field, and it ranks\Nwhat's worth re-testing…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.00,0:00:36.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,…then overlays, live, which claims were\Nindependently checked — and how they held.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.00,0:00:48.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,This one was checked: validated,\Ntraceable to a signed nanopublication.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.00,0:00:57.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,That verification layer is what\Na citation graph can't hold.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.00,0:01:13.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's the human view. Now the same engine\Nas an MCP — driven by an AI agent.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.00,0:01:28.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,The agent asks the Radar what's un-replicated.\NTop hit: a Nature marine-heatwave paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.00,0:01:36.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Highly cited — never independently checked.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.00,0:01:50.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Which software to reuse? It ranks real tools\Nby reuse signal and picks XMHW — independent.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.00,0:01:58.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,It even flags one that looks independent\Nbut is the author's own code.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.00,0:02:18.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,For data, it hands off to the OpenAIRE MCP —\Nan independent satellite dataset.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.00,0:02:24.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,A different producer from the original.\NA true replication, not a re-run.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.00,0:02:35.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,And it's honest: satellite data only reaches the\N1980s — the century-long trend stays an open question.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.00,0:02:46.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,It scaffolds the repo from the FORRT template\Nand records the paper, data, and software.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.00,0:02:49.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two MCPs on one Graph — discover, then check.\NThat's Replication Radar.
